 string contains a compatible pre-existing row in an unrelated table and has no application tables. when The application starts, initializes its database structures, and a contract operation reads or changes application data. then The unrelated row remains unchanged, the required application tables exist, and the response reflects persisted application data.\",\n    \"Given A contract operation creates or changes application data, including a value differing from the existing value. when The API completes the operation successfully. then The corresponding database row contains the submitted values and derived or cached values returned in the response.\",\n    \"Given A successful API mutation has been committed to the configured PostgreSQL database. when The API process restarts and a contract read operation retrieves that data. then The response fields contain the committed values from the database row.\",\n    \"Given A PostgreSQL test fixture contains an authorized principal established as test setup, an empty application-data state, and a contract operation valid for that principal that creates or changes an application record. when The client uses the contract operation and then reads the record through the corresponding API list or detail operation. then The response contains the saved value and a PostgreSQL row contains the same value.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When Seed:Demo is true at application startup on an initially clean database, the Feedlot Operations API shall run App.Api/SeedData.cs to populate each application table with demo rows based on believable examples from contracts/openapi.yaml.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A clean database is configured and Seed:Demo is true. when The application starts and a client requests each contract list operation. then Each response list count is at least one and the returned sample values include data drawn from contract examples.\",\n    \"Given The App database is empty and Seed:Demo is true. 