demo-data row count is zero and the list responses contain no demo rows.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The Feedlot Operations API shall expose only backend API and documentation surfaces, with no product-facing web application screens or frontend implementation in this repository.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given The repository implementation is complete. when A person reviews its exposed web surfaces and frontend files. then The review finds API and API documentation surfaces but no product-facing screens or frontend implementation.\",\n    \"Given The API application built from this repository. when A person inspects its browser-accessible surfaces. then The screen shows API health or API documentation and does not show feedlot product screens.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When a ration defines ingredient proportions, the Feedlot Operations API shall calculate ingredient consumption and ration cost from as-fed ingredient weights and use dry-matter values only for nutritional calculations.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A ration contains ingredients with stated proportions, different dry-matter percentages, and known unit costs. when A client records a feeding event and reads the ration and event results. then The response ingredient movement quantities and cost fields reflect the as-fed proportions and costs, while nutritional values reflect dry-matter values.\",\n    \"Given A ration has two ingredients with known as-fed unit costs and dry-matter percentages, with proportions of 70% and 30%, and a feeding request delivers 100 lb. when The feeding event is recorded successfully. then The response movement fields report 70 lb and 30 lb consumed, its cost fields equal the as-fed weighted cost, and its nutritional fields reflect the ingredients' dry-matter conversion.\",\n    \"Given A test-created ration whose ingredient proportions are percentages of as-fed weight, with different dry-matter percentages and known unit costs, and sufficient inventory. when The client records a feeding event through POST /api/feeding-events. then The response event shows each ingredient's consumed as-fed quantity and a cost equal to the sum of as-fed ingredient quantities multiplied by their unit costs, while nutrition values reflect dry-matter data.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When a feeding event is created or corrected, or a saved feeding event is voided, the Feedlot Operations API shall atomically reject any creation or correction requiring unavailable ingredient inventory without changing persisted event, inventory, movement, or lot feed-rollup values, apply successful corrections as replacements of the prior event's inventory and rollup effects, and reverse a voided event's inventory and rollup effects.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given An ingredient has less available inventory than a proposed feeding event requires and inventory and lot rollup values have been recorded. when The client posts the feeding event. then The response status is 409 and the inventory row, feeding-event row count, and lot feed totals remain unchanged.\",\n    \"Given Inventory contains less than the required quantity of at least one ingredient for a feeding event. when A client submits the event to the createFeedingEvent operation. then The response status is 409, no feeding-event row or inventory-movement row is added, and inventory quantities and lot feed and cost rollup values remain unchanged.\",\n    \"Given A test-created ration and inventory where one ingredient has less stock than the event requires, with recorded pre-request inventory and lot totals. when The client submits POST /api/feeding-events for that event. then The response status is 409, no event row exists for the rejected request, the inventory row values are unchanged, and the lot feed-total response values are unchanged.\",\n    \"Given A saved feeding event has an inventory movement and lot feed rollup values, and a proposed correction requires more of at least one ingredient than is available after accounting for the saved event's existing inventory effect. when The client submits the correction through PATCH /api/feeding-events/{eventId}. then The response status is 409, the saved event row and its inventory-movement rows remain unchanged, and the inventory row values and lot feed and cost rollup values remain unchanged.\",\n    \"Given A saved feeding event has an inventory movement and lot feed rollup values, and a valid correction changes the delivered quantity to a different quantity with sufficient inventory. when The client submits the correction through PATCH /api/feeding-events/{eventId}. then The response event and lotFeedTotals contain the corrected values, the event's inventory movements reflect only the corrected consumption, and the inventory row reflects the corrected net consumption rather than both the original and corrected quantities.\",\n    \"Given A saved feeding event has an inventory movement and lot feed rollup values. when The client voids the event through POST /api/feeding-events/{eventId}/void. then The response event status is Voided, its inventoryMovements include the reversal of the event's inventory consumption, the inventory row reflects the restored quantity, and the lotFeedTotals exclude the voided event's feed and cost.\",\n    \"Given Inventory has a known quantity of an ingredient, and two otherwise valid concurrent POST /api/feeding-events requests each require no more than that quantity individually but together require more than the available quantity. when The client sends both requests concurrently. then The two response statuses are one contract-declared success status and one 409; exactly one feeding-event row and its corresponding inventory-movement rows are added, and the inventory row equals the starting quantity minus the successful event's consumption and remains nonnegative.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When Days on Feed is zero, ADG is nonpositive, or no positive gain remains toward the target, the Feedlot Operations API shall return ADG, feed-to-gain metrics, and projected ship dates as unavailable whenever their required positive denominator or gain is absent.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A lot has zero Days on Feed, or has zero or negative total weight gain or ADG. when The client requests that lot's metrics. then The response fields for affected metrics and projectedShipDate contain null rather than a numeric value or date.\",\n    \"Given A lot has zero Days on Feed. when A client reads its lot metrics and lot list values. then The response adg and projectedShipDate fields are JSON null.\",\n    \"Given A lot has positive Days on Feed and zero or negative total weight gain. when A client reads its lot metrics, lot list, dashboard, and feed-to-gain report values. then The response adg, feedConversionRatio or fcr, costOfGain or costPerGain, and projectedShipDate fields are JSON null wherever those fields are exposed.\",\n    \"Given A lot has positive Days on Feed and positive total weight gain below its target weight. when A client reads its lot metrics after the latest weight measurement is recorded. then The response contains numeric values for applicable feed-to-gain metric fields and a projectedShipDate field calculated from the positive gain rate.\",\n    \"Given A test-created lot whose receiving date makes Days on Feed zero. when The client sends GET /api/lots/{lotId}/metrics. then The response field daysOnFeed is 0 and the response fields adg and projectedShipDate are null.\",\n    \"Given A test-created lot with positive Days on Feed and zero or negative total weight gain. when The client sends GET /api/lots/{lotId}/metrics. then The response fields feedConversionRatio and costOfGain are null, and projectedShipDate is null when ADG is zero or negative.\"\n   ]\n  }\n ],\n \"nfrs\": [\n  \"Every HTTP method and path declared in the locked OpenAPI contract conforms to its declared request, response, 